 - **A-W15 correction 6, `--yes` under tmux (planned text wrong).** Planned: state that `--yes` is not forwarded in tmux mode and recommend `--no-tmux` when using it. Code: `--yes` is indeed absent from `_build_foreground_command` (`src/superclaude/cli/sprint/tmux.py:176-217`), but the auto-resume confirmation that `--yes` answers runs in the outer process (`sprint/commands.py:323-337`) before `launch_in_tmux` (`commands.py:435-436`), and the inner argv carries an explicit `--start`, which disables auto-resume (`commands.py:319-322`). Written instead: `--yes` is not forwarded but not needed there; `--no-tmux` is recommended only for `--resume`, `--task-parallelism`, `--handoff/--no-handoff`.
 - **A-W15 correction 6, forwarded-flag precision.** The item's "`--stall-*`" is written as `--stall-timeout` (only when > 0) and `--stall-action` (only when not `warn`); `--startup-stall-timeout` is not forwarded (`tmux.py:206-209`). The guide also says any flag not in the forwarded list does not reach the inner worker.
 - **A-W15 adjacent fix in §4.2 (code-true).** The old line "`CLAUDECODE=\"\"` is injected into child env" was replaced: `build_env` removes `CLAUDECODE` and `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` (`src/superclaude/cli/pipeline/process.py:178-180`). The item's `:303`/`:320` `/sc:task-unified` fix also covered a fourth occurrence (the §4.3.1 "Command header" bullet) so the AC "no `/sc:task-unified`" holds.
